# Copy values into your OS or user environment (Cursor resolves ${env:...} in mcp.json).
# Remote MCP servers do not load envFile; set variables before launching Cursor, or define
# them in Windows "Environment variables" / macOS launchctl / CI secrets.
#
# Option A — Personal API token (Basic), after admin enables API token auth for Rovo MCP:
#   printf 'you@company.com:YOUR_ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN' | base64 -w0   # Linux
#   [Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes("you@company.com:TOKEN"))  # PowerShell
# Then set exactly:
#   ATLASSIAN_MCP_AUTHORIZATION=Basic <base64-output>
#
# Option B — Service account (Bearer):
#   ATLASSIAN_MCP_AUTHORIZATION=Bearer <service-account-api-key>
#
# Token creation (scopes): https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens
# Docs: https://support.atlassian.com/atlassian-rovo-mcp-server/docs/configuring-authentication-via-api-token/
#
# OAuth (interactive) instead of env: use Cursor Marketplace "Atlassian" and disable this
# block if you prefer browser consent — do not commit secrets to the repo.
